Z||000014||GREENDANO||01-30-2000||08:58 AM||||Chronic no start with my 85 GT, chased it for a week.  Found a bad fusible link at the positive junction right by the batter, you know, the one that get wet everytime it rains. No other problems in the three years I had it.  <BR>  Don't even get me started about my F40.......  Man, I'd like to meet the woodchuck that started this kit.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||wkayl||02-05-2000||01:15 AM||||I have an 86 1/2 GT.  I drove from Loveland CO to Fargo ND to have my cousin install remote start system. For pics of my trip go to:  <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/fierotrip.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/wkayl/fierotrip.html</A>   The next morning it wouldn't start.  I gave him the line all mechanics hear "Well, you just worked on it"  It was a bad ign coil.  Who would have thought putting a coil on an exhaust heat shield would make a coil fail. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||DJRice||02-07-2000||09:20 AM||||The only electric problem that I have is that I dont have electric windows or locks...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||ChadMan||02-07-2000||09:31 AM||||My 84 had a lot of electrical problems.  Twice it left me stranded (once in a snowstorm) because of blown fusible links.<P>But my 88 Coupe has never had any electrical problems.  Neither did my 86 SE or my father-in-law's 86 SE.||||reg||1
